Model Triangle_suppression
Title: COVID-19 Triangle suppression model
Description: This model is a novel approach to modeling the progression of the COVID-19 pandemic in the US and forecasting the outcome and durations of a suppression strategy over the course of the year 2020.~
~
The core idea behind the model is the assuption that a suppression strategy is the only viable option. This realization comes out of the <a href="https://doi.org/10.25561/77482">Imperial College COVID-19 Task Force report</a> that was released on 16-Mar-2020.  So as the only viable option, model assumes that a suppression stratety will have to be adopted eventually, the question is just when and how strictly it will be implemented.~
~
The ideas behind the model are described in depth in my article <a href="https://analytica.com/forecast-update-us-deaths-from-covid-19-coronavirus-in-2020/">Suppression strategy and update forecast for US deaths from COVID-19 Coronavirus in 2020</a>, published on the Analytica blog on 23-Mar-2020.
Author: Lonnie Chrisman, Ph.D.~
Lumina Decision Systems
Date: Sun, Mar 15, 2020 11:37 AM
DiagState: 2,75,13,962,498,17
WindState: 2,108,255,720,500
DiagramColor: 52427,56425,65535
FontStyle: Arial,15
