Function Plot_Tukey_bars(canv, info, roles : reduced ; showMean : boolean atom=false)
Title: Plot Tukey bars~
(canv, info, roles, showMean )
Description: Draws Tukey-bars on a graph that has a categorical X-axis and is displaying a probability bands graph.~
To use, set the OnGraphDraw attribute to:~
~
	continue := Plot_Tukey_bars( canv, info, roles, showMean:true )~
~
And set the flags for OnGraphDraw to "after axes, before data".  You don't have to include the showMean:true option, but when you do, the mean is also shown as a dot on the graph.~
~
To see the Tukey bars, view the Bands result view. Set Key to None and then set the .Probability slicer to «All», which eliminates the key. It is better without the key since the colors displayed in the key don't apply to this depiction of the data.
Definition: Local phase := info[OnGraphDrawItem='Phase'];~
LocalAlias main := info[OnGraphDrawItem='Result'];~
~
if info[OnGraphDrawItem='ViewMode']<>'Bands' or phase<4 ~
		{or info[OnGraphDrawItem='SwapXY']}~
		or handle(main) <> roles[GraphingRole='Y axis',GraphFillerInfo='Source']~
		or not roles[GraphingRole='X axis',GraphFillerInfo='Categorical']~
Then ~
	True ~
else begin~
	LocalAlias xCats := (roles[GraphingRole='X axis',GraphFillerInfo='Source']); ~
	Local yAxis := roles[GraphingRole='Y axis'];~
	Local val := #yAxis[GraphFillerInfo='Value'];~
	if SetContains( \IndexNames(val), ".Probability" ) Then (~
		Local clip := Clip_to_PlotArea(canv,info); ~
		OCD_Draw_tukey_bar( clip, info, roles, xCats, val, val.probability );~
		if showMean then (~
			OGD_Plot_points(clip,info,roles,Mean(main))~
		);~
		False~
	) else (~
		True~
	)~
end
NodeLocation: 296,100,1
