Module The_suppression_tria
Title: The suppression triangle
Description: The triangle suppression model is a novel approach to modeling the progression of COVID-19 in the US through the end of 2020. It is described in the article <a href="https://lumina.com/forecast-update-us-deaths-from-covid-19-coronavirus-in-2020/">Suppression strategy and update forecast for US deaths from COVID-19 Coronavirus in 2020</a>, and this module contains the model used in that article.
Author: Lonnie Chrisman, Ph.D.~
Lumina Decision Systems
Date: Sat, Mar 21, 2020 3:24 PM
NodeLocation: 160,176,1
NodeSize: 80,32
DiagState: 2,30,120,1047,552,17
WindState: 2,880,360,720,350

Chance Decay_rate_after_mea
Title: Decay rate after measures
Description: The probability distribution for the decay rate (a negative number) that will occur during the suppression phase. A value of zero would be a steady state (with no end to measures). Stronger lock down measures should result in a more negative value, and a more negative value ends the suppression phase faster.  The "reasonable" range of possible values is from -0.1 to 0.~
~
The units are in Ln(deaths) / day.~
~
In China, once the deaths peaked, the average growth rate from 18-Feb-2020 thru 16-Mar-2020 was -0.0975 (pretty close to -0.1).  This is while the recovery was ramping down.
Definition: Uniform(-0.1,0)
NodeLocation: 104,248,1
NodeSize: 48,32
WindState: 2,949,360,720,350
ValueState: 2,181,495,450,345,1,XCDZ
Aliases: FormNode Fo955920189
GraphSetup: {!40400|Sys_PdfSmoothMethod:1}~
Att_ContLineStyle Graph_Pdf_Valdim:1

Chance Delay_to_start_effec
Title: Delay to start effect
Units: days
Description: A probability distribution for the lag time (number of days) between when suppression measures start and the effect as a reduction in daily deaths becomes observable.~
~
In China, there was an 11 day lag between new reported cases and deaths, and a 27 day lag from the lockdown of Wuhan city until the peak of death.
Definition: UncertainLMH( 11, 14, 18, lb:2, ub:30 );
NodeLocation: 368,272,1
NodeSize: 48,24
WindState: 2,903,454,720,350
ValueState: 2,807,307,430,317,,PDFP
Aliases: FormNode Fo298200893
GraphSetup: {!40400|Sys_PdfSmoothMethod:1}~
DistSteps:1

Variable Growth_rate_by_time
Title: Growth rate by time
Definition: if Time < Effective_date_of_ac + Delay_to_start_effec ~
Then Cur_Growth_rate ~
Else If Decay_rate_treatment = 'Use distribution' Then Decay_rate_after_mea~
Else Decay_rate_levels
